cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "Benchmark-aware regional validation of a reproducible WGS variant-calling workflow using GIAB HG001 chr22 reference regions"

message: "If you use this repository or derived analyses, please cite this work."

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Rawat
    given-names: Ritika Rajendra

repository-code: "https://github.com/Rita1791/Benchmark-aware-WGS-preventive-genomics"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - whole-genome sequencing
  - WGS
  - variant calling
  - Genome in a Bottle
  - GIAB
  - HG001
  - NA12878
  - GRCh38
  - chromosome 22
  - bcftools
  - RTG vcfeval
  - benchmarking
  - bioinformatics

abstract: >
  A reproducible benchmark-aware workflow for regional validation of
  whole-genome sequencing variant calling using GIAB HG001/NA12878
  and GRCh38 chromosome 22 high-confidence regions. The workflow
  combines normalized bcftools isec comparison, formal RTG vcfeval
  benchmarking, benchmark-scale evaluation, and systematic analysis
  of missed variants and difficult genomic regions.
